{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"hexametric-antique-blowfish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nGerrit review of change 1536 confirmed the new locked commit-and-push entrypoint safely fails closed when local lock-artifact exclusion cannot be installed, and that the pre-lock update may append harmless duplicate exclude lines under concurrent first use. Preserve the shipped compatibility contract while tightening the local metadata update and its direct failure oracles.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Characterize modern and legacy tracker ignore behavior, including concurrent first use.\n- Make the local exclude update idempotent/atomic where practical without moving it behind the recovery guard or allowing lock artifacts into commits.\n- Add direct tests for exclusion-write failure and git-status failure under strict/default modes, plus explicit proof that reserved lock artifacts never enter the committed tree.\n- Preserve the existing stage-failed reason, best-effort warning/return behavior, clean retry, and push-only compatibility.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Concurrent first use cannot corrupt local exclude metadata; duplicate-line disposition is documented or eliminated.\n- [ ] Strict and default exclusion/status failures are directly covered with observable typed-error or warning/return outcomes.\n- [ ] A real legacy tracker commit proves lock artifacts are absent from the resulting commit and a clean retry succeeds.\n- [ ] Existing push-only and commit-and-push compatibility suites remain green.","id":"210c-b695-f0a3-46e4","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["store","concurrency","testing"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Harden lock-artifact exclusion metadata and failure coverage"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786163034106637001,"uuid":"6345b179-851c-4277-879a-d77f9ef5b4d6"}